ruben@dat.etsit.upm.es  writes:
> hi everybody.
> I have recently got the game Master of Magic and I have a little mess.
> When I start in the city, I send out my barbarian unit and they die because 
> they don't have enough food.
> How can they have enough food? (Then program says that I should build farms,
> but I don't know how)
> I would thank a lot any kind of help.
> 	See you!    Ruben.

When the message comes up "Not enough food...", answer no.
Then go to the city that has the best production and
right-click on it.  When in the city screen, go to the
population section (upper-left line of people).  The left-most
people will be "farmers".  There will be a space somewhere in
that line which I think stands for the amount of farmers needed
to support the city.  Find the first (from the left side)
person that is a different icon from the farmer (excluding
those in revolt) and left-click just to the left of him to
change him to a farmer.  If you don't have any "workers", find
another city and repeat the process.  After all of this is
done, you need to make a decision concerning future
production.  I generally start a granary, farmer's market, or
something else that increases food production.  If this isn't
possible, then you have to stop producing military units.
BTW- Every other time that a city changes size, it needs more
food and is likely to cause the old "out of food" message.

